Debezium 3.1.3.Final, PostgreSQL connector: stop probing the SNAPSHOT connection
while streaming waits for a blocking snapshot. This is upstream's own revert
(debezium/debezium cd2b1b3013, "DBZ-8680 Revert ...", first shipped in 3.2.0),
reduced to its one-line production change. There is no 3.1.4.

Why: in 3.1.0-3.1.3, streaming paused for a blocking snapshot runs `SELECT 1` +
`commit()` every status.update.interval.ms (10 s) on the JDBC connection the
snapshot is reading through. The commit closes the snapshot's server-side
cursor, the next fetch fails with `portal "C_n" does not exist`, the snapshot
aborts, streaming resumes, and the connector stays RUNNING -- so every CDC
Reload of a PostgreSQL table whose export outlives one probe tick silently
loses rows. Applied by the kafka-connect Dockerfile (stage dbz-pg-patch).

Modified from the Apache-2.0 licensed Debezium source (Copyright Debezium
Authors); the change is the hunk below.

diff --git a/debezium-connector-postgres/src/main/java/io/debezium/connector/postgresql/PostgresStreamingChangeEventSource.java b/debezium-connector-postgres/src/main/java/io/debezium/connector/postgresql/PostgresStreamingChangeEventSource.java
--- a/debezium-connector-postgres/src/main/java/io/debezium/connector/postgresql/PostgresStreamingChangeEventSource.java
+++ b/debezium-connector-postgres/src/main/java/io/debezium/connector/postgresql/PostgresStreamingChangeEventSource.java
@@ -260,14 +260,7 @@ && haveNotReceivedStreamingStoppingLsn(offsetContext, lastCompletelyProcessedLsn
             if (context.isPaused()) {
                 LOGGER.info("Streaming will now pause");
                 context.streamingPaused();
-                context.waitSnapshotCompletion(() -> {
-                    try {
-                        probeConnectionIfNeeded();
-                    }
-                    catch (SQLException e) {
-                        throw new DebeziumException(e);
-                    }
-                });
+                context.waitSnapshotCompletion();
                 LOGGER.info("Streaming resumed");
             }
         }
